"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, Pickaway County has 75 years of record from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids February to March came in under 90% of normal in 35 of them. In 2025 August to September ran 53% of normal on the middle, while May to June ran 159%. Grid 23290 had its driest year in 1987 at 61% of normal. A preliminary estimate for grid 23888 puts August to September 2026 at 241.7, and that figure can still change.</p>"}
